  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bfcb709b487afd749b8fbd2c4c50e261, type: 3}
  m_Name: Cleric
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Key: Cleric
  Vision:
    Fantasy: A devout healer. Will prioritise others over herself, with the strongest
      focus being on healing and support.
    Role: The strongest backline healer. Almost everything scales of spirit, perhaps
      a few offensive spells off int AND spirit.
    SignatureMechanic: Is the main source for reviving, although most likely not
      the only one. However, should be the only one with access to mass-revive.
    UltraStyle: Miracles
    Ultras:
    - Name: Miracle of Light
      Effect: Heals the party and clears every debuff. (full heal is too powerful
        i think)
      Unlock: a
    - Name: Miracle of Hope
      Effect: Every hero regains 1 ability charge. (can be upgraded to give more
        charges, but  costly)
      Unlock: b
    - Name: Miracle of Righteousness
      Effect: Holy damage to every enemy; Undead under 30% health are destroyed outright.
        (excluding bosses)
      Unlock: c
    Branches:
    - GridBranch: a
      Becomes: A pure healer with ensuring others stay topped off.
      IntendedKit: A direct heal => a magic shield => regen => Revive
      Summon: 'Phoenix - special attack: Mass revive and heal (both start out at
        low %)'
    - GridBranch: b
      Becomes: A more supportive role with aim on tempo improvements
      IntendedKit: Sanctuary (+Endurance % to all) => Inspire (restore 1 ability
        charge to one hero) => Quicken (Haste on one ally)
      Summon: 'Guardian Angel - special attack: Protective shield for X% of total
        health to all + endurance buff'
    - GridBranch: c
      Becomes: Holy damage dealer with extra damage to undead type of enemies
      IntendedKit: Divine Bolt => Purge (Holy to all, double vs Undead) => Searing
        Light (Holy + Silence)
      Summon: 'Archon - party replacement: A replacement summon, oriented around
        holy damage'
    Overlaps: Paladin on healing
    OpenQuestions: Revive and mass revive need a new effect type. Holy-vs-Undead
      needs enemies tagged Undead (UnitTraits exists, nothing is tagged yet). Her
      grid today (Heal, Renew, Benediction, Smite, Ward) predates this vision and
      gets rebuilt to it.
